Experimental source-owned startup extension dispatch; not automatically applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006 bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires prior caller/auth/refusal/restricted/catalog/settings/empty-auth/presence/telemetry/marketplace/logging/plugin-roots patches.
Modules: extensions/runner::{raceHandlerWithTimeout,ExtensionRunner.emit,addExtensions}; CLI and SDK exact-session binding.
Tests: startup-extension-owner.test.ts and existing extensions-runner, SDK and CLI suites.
Difference: --startup-extension requires --restrict-tools and binds the exact runner;
it joins original session_start handlers and observers, refuses timeout and failure,
rejects repeated dispatch or additions, and emits a one-use identity-bound receipt
outside the handler. Ordinary extension behavior remains available without the flag.
Other extension work, complete inventory, Ready, paid execution, signing and release remain open.

